WEBVTT

1
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:34.375
<b>In this final verse of the third chapter,</b>

2
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:39.750
<b>Lord Krishna is concluding </b>
<b>His discussion on desire.</b>

3
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.875
<b>He explains that spiritual knowledge is </b>
<b>the primary means to conquer desire.</b>

4
00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.750
<b>Naturally, the question arises:</b>

5
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.541
<b>how does one attain this knowledge?</b>

6
00:00:50.541 --> 00:00:53.541
<b>This will be detailed in the fourth chapter.</b>

7
00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:03.375
<b>Here, Lord Krishna emphasizes </b>
<b>developing spiritual knowledge.</b>

8
00:01:03.375 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>He states that spiritual knowledge </b>
<b>strengthens one's intellect,</b>

9
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.583
<b>and this very intellect will </b>
<b>help in conquering desire.</b>

10
00:01:13.583 --> 00:01:16.875
<b>But what is this knowledge?</b>

11
00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:24.000
<b>Spiritual knowledge is understanding</b>
<b>that our true existence is the soul,</b>

12
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
<b>which transcends the senses, mind, and intellect.</b>

13
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.875
<b>And in previous verses, we learned</b>

14
00:01:30.875 --> 00:01:36.208
<b>that desire resides in all three—</b>
<b>the senses, mind, and intellect.</b>

15
00:01:36.208 --> 00:01:41.625
<b>So, consistently losing to desire means</b>
<b>losing to insignificant materialism,</b>

16
00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:44.458
<b>which is entirely inappropriate.</b>

17
00:01:44.458 --> 00:01:49.291
<b>Here, Krishna addresses Arjuna as "Maha-baho,"</b>

18
00:01:49.291 --> 00:01:52.958
<b>meaning one with mighty arms.</b>

19
00:01:52.958 --> 00:01:54.958
<b>It's as if He's saying,</b>

20
00:01:54.958 --> 00:02:01.708
<b>"O Arjuna, with these powerful arms you</b>
<b>have conquered many external enemies,</b>

21
00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:06.791
<b>and now you must conquer this</b>
<b>internal enemy called desire.</b>

22
00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:13.875
<b>But the difference is, in this internal battle, </b>
<b>these arms won't help you.</b>

23
00:02:13.875 --> 00:02:22.750
<b>In this battle, if anything will support you, </b>
<b>it's your intellect and your spiritual faith,</b>

24
00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.166
<b>which will remain steady</b>

25
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:29.458
<b>only when you know your true </b>
<b>existence as this soul."</b>

26
00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:33.541
<b>But what meaning can we all </b>
<b>derive from this in our lives?</b>

27
00:02:33.541 --> 00:02:37.666
<b>Simply this: when we develop </b>
<b>our spiritual knowledge,</b>

28
00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:42.916
<b>we'll realize that we're not this material body, </b>
<b>but we are a soul.</b>

29
00:02:42.916 --> 00:02:47.250
<b>And this very awareness will </b>
<b>inspire us toward spirituality,</b>

30
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:52.041
<b>and ultimately, we'll rise above </b>
<b>the influence of desire.</b>

31
00:02:52.041 --> 00:02:56.958
<b>But if we remain in the misconception </b>
<b>that we are this body,</b>

32
00:02:56.958 --> 00:03:04.416
<b>it's natural that for this body's pleasure, </b>
<b>many material cravings will arise within us.</b>

33
00:03:04.416 --> 00:03:06.166
<b>This indeed is desire.</b>

34
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:07.833
<b>We must exercise control,</b>

35
00:03:07.833 --> 00:03:11.250
<b>which was explained in detail in previous verses.</b>

36
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.291
<b>Second,</b>

37
00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:15.458
<b>we must develop our spiritual knowledge.</b>

38
00:03:15.458 --> 00:03:21.750
<b>And the development of this knowledge </b>
<b>is explained extensively in the fourth chapter.</b>

39
00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.875
<b>Therefore,</b>

40
00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:26.500
<b>stay with this Bhagavad Gita.</b>

41
00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:34.083
<b>Desire is an enemy,</b>

42
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:35.833
<b>and Arjuna is</b>

43
00:03:35.833 --> 00:03:38.166
<b>Maha-baho.</b>

44
00:03:38.166 --> 00:03:41.416
<b>He must defeat this enemy.</b>

45
00:03:41.416 --> 00:03:45.958
<b>After all, this too is like a battle,</b>

46
00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:50.750
<b>one that exists within Arjuna, within you.</b>

47
00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:58.083
<b>A battle that every person </b>
<b>fights against their desires.</b>

48
00:03:58.083 --> 00:04:06.583
<b>Just as physical weapons are needed to </b>
<b>defeat external enemies on the battlefield,</b>

49
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:08.291
<b>similarly,</b>

50
00:04:08.291 --> 00:04:13.750
<b>this internal war will require spiritual weapons.</b>

51
00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:21.083
<b>And this weapon is your spiritual knowledge.</b>

52
00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:30.916
<b>And this knowledge is accepting the truth that </b>
<b>we are all fundamentally spiritual beings.</b>

53
00:04:30.916 --> 00:04:36.125
<b>A being in which the soul resides.</b>

54
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:44.916
<b>And our true identity transcends the body, </b>
<b>its senses, and their experiences.</b>

55
00:04:44.916 --> 00:04:51.041
<b>When you begin to understand </b>
<b>that you are not just this body,</b>

56
00:04:51.041 --> 00:04:56.458
<b>but the soul that dwells </b>
<b>within this bodily covering,</b>

57
00:04:56.458 --> 00:05:03.291
<b>this perspective transforms </b>
<b>your relationship with the world.</b>

58
00:05:03.291 --> 00:05:07.291
<b>When you consider yourself merely the body,</b>

59
00:05:07.291 --> 00:05:16.208
<b>your goals and desires revolve only around </b>
<b>physical pleasures and sensory experiences.</b>

60
00:05:16.208 --> 00:05:19.041
<b>Such desires are endless,</b>

61
00:05:19.041 --> 00:05:28.208
<b>like a maze where fulfilling </b>
<b>one desire awakens another,</b>

62
00:05:28.208 --> 00:05:34.833
<b>and this cycle of desire continues endlessly.</b>

63
00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:45.125
<b>One trapped in this cycle finds only </b>
<b>dissatisfaction and sorrow.</b>

64
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:47.583
<b>This is the essence of desire –</b>

65
00:05:47.583 --> 00:05:52.583
<b>whether physical or any other material craving.</b>

66
00:05:52.583 --> 00:05:53.708
<b>However,</b>

67
00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:58.708
<b>when you begin to see yourself as a soul,</b>

68
00:05:58.708 --> 00:06:01.416
<b>your perspective changes.</b>

69
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:08.958
<b>You understand that these material </b>
<b>desires can never give you true satisfaction.</b>

70
00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:14.083
<b>If you're thirsty, what good will </b>
<b>sprinkling water on the house do?</b>

71
00:06:14.083 --> 00:06:15.416
<b>Similarly,</b>

72
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:17.958
<b>if you seek soul's satisfaction,</b>

73
00:06:17.958 --> 00:06:24.333
<b>satisfying its bodily house will achieve nothing.</b>

74
00:06:24.333 --> 00:06:31.708
<b>Studying spiritual texts, participating </b>
<b>in philosophical and moral discussions,</b>

75
00:06:31.708 --> 00:06:37.041
<b>and contemplating the nature </b>
<b>of your true existence –</b>

76
00:06:37.041 --> 00:06:40.666
<b>all this strengthens your intellect</b>

77
00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:45.125
<b>and increases your spiritual awareness.</b>

78
00:06:45.125 --> 00:06:46.500
<b>And ultimately,</b>

79
00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.041
<b>the benefits of all these manifest in daily life.</b>

80
00:06:51.041 --> 00:06:54.708
<b>You begin to rise above trivial desires.</b>

81
00:06:54.708 --> 00:07:04.250
<b>You channel your energy into actions </b>
<b>that bring deeper satisfaction</b>

82
00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.416
<b>and peace to the soul, rather </b>
<b>than momentary pleasure.</b>

83
00:07:07.416 --> 00:07:11.833
<b>You gradually become a better human being.</b>

84
00:07:11.833 --> 00:07:16.041
<b>There is a unique joy in such a life.</b>

85
00:07:16.041 --> 00:07:19.333
<b>Try walking on this path.</b>

86
00:07:24.125 --> 00:07:26.000
<b>Viewing desire</b>

87
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:29.833
<b>and other trivial cravings as enemies,</b>

88
00:07:29.833 --> 00:07:36.958
<b>and using spiritual knowledge </b>
<b>as a weapon to conquer them –</b>

89
00:07:36.958 --> 00:07:41.458
<b>this understanding is valuable in </b>
<b>the family environment.</b>

90
00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:43.500
<b>When family members</b>

91
00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:49.208
<b>see themselves and others </b>
<b>not just in physical form,</b>

92
00:07:49.208 --> 00:07:53.708
<b>but in their spiritual form,</b>

93
00:07:53.708 --> 00:08:03.541
<b>naturally the conflicts arising from material </b>
<b>desires like money, wealth, ego and such</b>

94
00:08:03.541 --> 00:08:05.375
<b>begin to diminish.</b>

95
00:08:05.375 --> 00:08:07.208
<b>And in its place,</b>

96
00:08:07.208 --> 00:08:13.375
<b>a mutual understanding emerges </b>
<b>that seeks only the good of others.</b>

97
00:08:13.375 --> 00:08:15.958
<b>To create such an environment,</b>

98
00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:19.750
<b>families must participate in activities</b>

99
00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:25.208
<b>that encourage self-realization </b>
<b>and spiritual knowledge.</b>

100
00:08:25.208 --> 00:08:30.500
<b>Such as studying spiritual texts </b>
<b>together as a family,</b>

101
00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.958
<b>discussing philosophical questions,</b>

102
00:08:32.958 --> 00:08:37.458
<b>or participating in social service.</b>

103
00:08:37.458 --> 00:08:43.875
<b>These activities will not only help build </b>
<b>a solid foundation of spiritual knowledge</b>

104
00:08:43.875 --> 00:08:44.625
<b>but</b>

105
00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:52.791
<b>will also encourage family members </b>
<b>to view life from a proper perspective.</b>

106
00:08:52.791 --> 00:08:57.416
<b>And to inspire the family toward such activities, </b>

107
00:08:57.416 --> 00:09:01.875
<b>parents and other elders must take the initiative.</b>

108
00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:06.500
<b>Children learn much by observing their parents.</b>

109
00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.875
<b>They unconsciously begin to follow them.</b>

110
00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:16.083
<b>Over time, this will strengthen such </b>
<b>beautiful thinking in the family,</b>

111
00:09:16.083 --> 00:09:18.791
<b>where children won't view the control </b>

112
00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:25.541
<b>of unnecessary desires and passions </b>
<b>negatively as restrictions.</b>

113
00:09:25.541 --> 00:09:28.750
<b>Instead, they will understand the importance</b>

114
00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:36.958
<b>of this control for a purposeful and satisfying life.</b>

115
00:09:36.958 --> 00:09:41.666
<b>Try beginning with the</b>
<b>collective study of this very Gita.</b>

116
00:09:41.666 --> 00:09:44.916
<b>Change will surely become visible.</b>

117
00:09:44.916 --> 00:09:46.583
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

118
00:09:51.375 --> 00:09:58.750
<b>Can spiritual knowledge be effective</b>
<b>in modern workplaces?</b>

119
00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:02.458
<b>This might sound strange to many,</b>

120
00:10:02.458 --> 00:10:03.458
<b>but</b>

121
00:10:03.458 --> 00:10:05.166
<b>that's precisely the point –</b>

122
00:10:05.166 --> 00:10:09.250
<b>we're so trapped in material desires</b>

123
00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:14.208
<b>that even what's good for us seems strange.</b>

124
00:10:14.208 --> 00:10:15.875
<b>Imagine</b>

125
00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:26.916
<b>a workplace where people are dutiful,</b>
<b>work with concentration and honesty.</b>

126
00:10:26.916 --> 00:10:30.250
<b>What a beautiful vision this is.</b>

127
00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:34.000
<b>And this vision can indeed become reality.</b>

128
00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.083
<b>Because</b>

129
00:10:35.083 --> 00:10:41.166
<b>spiritual knowledge teaches these very values.</b>

130
00:10:41.166 --> 00:10:47.625
<b>Certain measures can be taken to </b>
<b>create such a professional environment.</b>

131
00:10:47.625 --> 00:10:53.666
<b>Employees can be encouraged </b>
<b>to participate in programs</b>

132
00:10:53.666 --> 00:10:59.750
<b>that include study of moral and spiritual topics.</b>

133
00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:00.958
<b>These programs</b>

134
00:11:00.958 --> 00:11:06.458
<b>will inspire them to deeply understand </b>
<b>and apply the principles of integrity and duty</b>

135
00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:11.541
<b>in their professional lives.</b>

136
00:11:11.541 --> 00:11:16.666
<b>Just as you understood the </b>
<b>hierarchy of human consciousness,</b>

137
00:11:16.666 --> 00:11:21.041
<b>where at the lowest level are the senses,</b>

138
00:11:21.041 --> 00:11:26.875
<b>controlled by the mind, then intellect,</b>

139
00:11:26.875 --> 00:11:28.625
<b>and ultimately</b>

140
00:11:28.625 --> 00:11:31.833
<b>the soul, which is supreme.</b>

141
00:11:31.833 --> 00:11:36.791
<b>You also learned that the </b>
<b>soul's satisfaction is supreme,</b>

142
00:11:36.791 --> 00:11:40.250
<b>that alone brings joy to humans.</b>

143
00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:48.791
<b>This knowledge also inspires that humans should</b>
<b>work not for momentary sensory desires,</b>

144
00:11:48.791 --> 00:11:49.750
<b>but</b>

145
00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.583
<b>for the elevation of the soul.</b>

146
00:11:53.583 --> 00:11:55.958
<b>A form of this knowledge</b>

147
00:11:55.958 --> 00:11:59.583
<b>applies in the professional environment too.</b>

148
00:11:59.583 --> 00:12:05.083
<b>Where people working in an </b>
<b>organization begin to understand</b>

149
00:12:05.083 --> 00:12:12.250
<b>that the supreme purpose is the </b>
<b>organization's elevation, not personal gain.</b>

150
00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:13.791
<b>Here,</b>

151
00:12:13.791 --> 00:12:18.708
<b>here leadership plays a crucial role here.</b>

152
00:12:18.708 --> 00:12:25.541
<b>If senior officers themselves </b>
<b>become symbols of ethics and truth,</b>

153
00:12:25.541 --> 00:12:30.333
<b>if they themselves follow spiritual values,</b>

154
00:12:30.333 --> 00:12:36.416
<b>its impact will not only affect their </b>
<b>personal professional sphere</b>

155
00:12:36.416 --> 00:12:37.583
<b>but</b>

156
00:12:37.583 --> 00:12:42.125
<b>will influence all people working there.</b>

157
00:12:42.125 --> 00:12:48.375
<b>In some cases, the professional environment</b>
<b>becomes like a family.</b>

158
00:12:48.375 --> 00:12:52.250
<b>Just as children learn from parents,</b>

159
00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.333
<b>similarly</b>

160
00:12:53.333 --> 00:13:01.750
<b>in an organization, employees follow </b>
<b>those in leadership positions.</b>

161
00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.500
<b>For example –</b>

162
00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:08.708
<b>if any senior officer shows no </b>
<b>ego about their position,</b>

163
00:13:08.708 --> 00:13:16.291
<b>treats everyone with gentleness, </b>
<b>all will adopt this nature.</b>

164
00:13:16.291 --> 00:13:18.208
<b>Now think,</b>

165
00:13:18.208 --> 00:13:19.791
<b>all these values –</b>

166
00:13:19.791 --> 00:13:25.916
<b>integrity, absence of ego, keeping focus on work,</b>

167
00:13:25.916 --> 00:13:30.583
<b>staying away from momentary </b>
<b>desires and passion.</b>

168
00:13:30.583 --> 00:13:37.083
<b>Aren't all these values necessary </b>
<b>for any organization?</b>

169
00:13:37.083 --> 00:13:39.250
<b>They certainly are.</b>

170
00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:48.708
<b>Therefore, encouraging spiritual knowledge</b>
<b>in an organization will only be beneficial,</b>

171
00:13:48.708 --> 00:13:50.541
<b>not strange.</b>

172
00:13:50.541 --> 00:13:53.708
<b>Reflect on this matter.</b>

